  "notes": "Minor-key melodic electro/future-house with a darker cast than tropical house. The research hands over the single most useful parameter in the entry as a direct quote: he \"focuses on melody and vocals over elements such as drums or bass\". That is encoded literally — the perc bed sits at 0-2 hits a bar at -8 dB, the quietest in this section; the hat fill density is 0.25; the bass is \"intentionally understated — a sidechained sub supporting the lead rather than competing with it\", at 0.96 roots in a narrow low register; and against all that the melody carries the arrangement, stating the hook in the intro and again as the drop. The tonality is documented rather than inferred: \"significantly darker and closer to minor keys compared to the upbeat rhythms of contemporary tropical house\", with four-chord i-VI-III-VII vamps and \"grandiose, emotionally-pitched melodies\", so the minor weighting is 7:2 and no major scale appears. He works in FL Studio with reFX Nexus, which he says \"defines the entirety of his sound\", hence the plucked/bell lead timbre; loops are 8 bars and his cited influences are film composers and video-game music. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the velocity tiers, the perc and roll densities and the registers.",
